# Build context for node/Dockerfile and router/Dockerfile. Both COPY the whole `scripts`
# directory because it is a workspace member and `cargo build` needs it to resolve the
# workspace — but the images only ever run `gas-killer-node` and `gas-killer-router`, which
# read none of its data files. Without these exclusions, editing an example manifest or a
# generated scenario invalidates the COPY layer and forces a full recompile of every image.
scripts/examples/
scripts/scenarios/

# Host-side checkout of gas-killer/example-contracts, fetched by scripts/examples/fetch_examples.sh
# with its nested submodules. Hundreds of MB, and the images never read it.
.examples/

# Compiled artifacts. The builder stage compiles inside a BuildKit cache mount, so a host
# target/ directory in the context is dead weight.
target/

# Never ship credentials into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
